  "description": "QIZTEC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H101 Fe7 N6 O40 Pr4,2.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 29 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.937-4.001 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.02-135.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Fe7Pr4(μ4-O)3(μ3-O)(μ3-OH)2(μ2-OH)(mdea)(κ1-OAc)(κ2-OAc)(μ-OAc)(H2O)]·2.5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
